    [" C5/L3 binding-position criterion language/module/resolve-binding (Open): Consume actual expanded syntax and its namespace/hygiene/macro context after expansion and before type/effect checking; every executable or declarative symbol resolves to an explicit identity or diagnostic. Use actual lexical stack, recur/function bindings, namespace, aliases, required/foreign tables, profile-allowed core imports, active profile/target, package graph and language facets. Preserve L3 unqualified expression order: lexical, recur/parameter, current namespace, profile-permitted core; macro/special forms use their syntactic positions. Alias-qualified and fully qualified names bypass that unqualified search and resolve through the actual alias/namespace/foreign records. C5's local/recur/namespace/alias-qualified/fully-qualified/core/foreign/intrinsic cases remain distinct eligible contexts; intrinsics require explicit syntax, macro positions prefer macro bindings over expression vars, and type/protocol positions use the type namespace. Required outputs: syntax-to-binding table and scope graph with positive local/namespace/alias/fully-qualified/macro/type/foreign/intrinsic and legal-shadowing fixtures. Reject unresolved/ambiguous names, illegal shadowing, missing/duplicate aliases and invented host bindings with C5-UNRESOLVED/AMBIGUOUS/SHADOW/ALIAS and applicable L3 diagnostics, retaining the actual resolved/candidate identities."
     " C5/L3 import/visibility criterion compiler/c5/explicit-imports language/module/enforce-export-visibility (Open): Resolve Gravity requires and foreign imports only from actual module artifacts, package manifests or explicit typed foreign/interop records; never inspect ambient host namespaces/globals or fabricate a dependency identity. Preserve profile, target, effects, capability requirements, safety, package/version and build-effect metadata on imports. Public API is the exported set plus package-public declarations; unexported definitions remain private, and debug/provenance visibility or an inspection grant does not authorize stable public import. Required outputs: actual alias/import/export tables, public API manifest, checked foreign records and positive/refused visibility/import fixtures. Reject absent/private/ambiguous names, stable-module wildcard imports, malformed foreign records, unsupported targets, unavailable required capabilities and missing metadata with C5-PRIVATE/ALIAS/FOREIGN/TARGET/CAPABILITY and L3-UNKNOWN-ALIAS/PRIVATE-IMPORT/AMBIGUOUS-NAME. The existing PKG1 entrypoint predicate remains unchanged; package retrieval and interop implementation are separate producers, not prerequisites for declared artifact fixtures or authority inferred from lookup."
     " C5/L3 namespace/initialization criterion language/module/check-initialization-graph (Open): Record the namespace contract for each normal source file's single ns, actual name/package/profile/target/source-path identity, one active implementation profile or declared reusable-library profile set with per-profile exclusions/variants, requested targets, requires/imports/exports, effect allowance, required capabilities, default safety and selected providers. Library support sets cannot union profile powers; target selection cannot legalize a forbidden profile behavior or claim core portability for a target-specific import. Emit versioned dependency and initialization edges. Reject cycles unless a declared checked recursive/module-initialization protocol explicitly admits them. Same-profile edges still require legal effects/authority; cross-profile edges require an actual pure-core API, profile-safe facade, typed schema/artifact, FFI ownership/effect/capability/safety boundary or generated artifact consumed through package metadata. Record boundary kind and missing evidence; runtime availability alone is insufficient and artifact consumption is not a source-import grant. Required outputs: namespace/dependency/initialization graphs, cross-profile edge and declaration/authority reports, accepted core/firmware and refused hosted-UI/kernel fixtures, cycle/protocol and profile cases. Preserve declared effect allowances and capability requests for actual Effects/Auth/profile/safety consumers; actual inferred summaries must fit declarations and package/deployment/build grants, with widening or absent authority rejected rather than treating resolution success as semantic approval. Emit C5-CYCLE/CROSS-PROFILE/TARGET/CAPABILITY and L3-NS-MISSING/PROFILE-MULTIPLE/CROSS-PROFILE/EFFECT-WIDEN/CAPABILITY-MISSING at the owning stage."
     " C5/L3 definition/interface criterion language/module/publish-definition-entries language/module/emit-reproducible-interface (Open): Publish actual expanded/analyzed def/defn/defmacro/defschema/defprotocol/facet entries with name, distinct kind, visibility, source span, type references, latent effects, required capabilities, profile restrictions, safety mode, artifact links and present deprecation/stability metadata. Binding records retain namespace/package/version/relevant profile-target/definition-kind/visibility/source and definition-artifact identity; binding IDs depend on semantic definition fields, excluding documentation/nonsemantic formatting while retaining separate exact provenance. Namespace identity cannot collapse to its name alone. Emit a reproducible/content-addressable module interface before target lowering with namespace/package/profile/target, aliases/exports/local-scope hash/syntax-binding map, requires including boundary/effect/authority facts, explicit foreign imports/rejected edges, diagnostics, source hash and definition identity. Actual backend/MIR/package consumers derive dependency/capability graphs, docs and conformance targets without rereading source. Required outputs: serialized namespace/binding/scope/module/public-API artifacts and stable index/invalidation records. Invalidate on namespace source, imports/exports, aliases, dependency versions, visibility, kind, profile/target set, language facets or macro-altered symbol positions, explicitly naming affected downstream artifacts/rechecks. Positive fixtures retain semantic binding identity across formatting while updating accurate source/artifact provenance; reject stale exports/keys, missing metadata, incompatible reused identities and unrecorded downstream invalidation."
     " C5/L3 consumer/conformance criterion (Open): Connect actual C3/C4 expanded-context and L1/L2 namespace-form inputs, explicit package/profile/foreign artifacts and resulting bindings to Core/Types/Effects/Auth/profile checks, package graphs, documentation/LSP and incremental consumers. Namespace tables precede expansion where required by L3; final symbol binding follows expanded positions under C5, and unresolved references cannot enter Types. Declared type/effect/authority records remain distinct from actual later inference/legality results; all required module summaries and facts must be current before target consumption. Required outputs: real producer/consumer and serialization/invalidation results covering every C5/L3 resolution position, stable binding identity, single-profile/multi-profile library exclusions, public/private and foreign imports, legal/refused shadowing, graph/cross-profile/target/capability cases and source-free package graph derivation. Preserve all ten C5 diagnostic meanings and all eight L3 meanings, with symbol/syntax ID/span/namespace/profile/target/candidate-bindings-when-applicable/dependency-edge/remediation context. Namespace-rule changes require conformance-fixture updates and package compatibility review under their owning policies; this source reconciliation changes no language rule. Preserve the separate frozen owner source-to-Core verification package and its finite scope. These are future implementation/evidence requirements, not current resolver/module/profile/package/runtime/probe execution, whole-component acceptance or independent source approval."]}
